			"notes": "**Alchemistry 1.0.4 — Minecraft 26.2**\n\nThis release fixes recipe locking, reactor automation, and machine processing issues.\n\n- Fixed the compactor locking its previous recipe when a new target was selected while paused. Targets now resolve immediately, even before ingredients are inserted.\n- Fixed the combiner carrying progress into a different recipe. Selecting the same recipe still preserves progress.\n- Fixed item duplication when breaking reactor input or output ports.\n- Fixed item loss when canceled automation transfers involved multiple reactor ports.\n- Fixed cached item and energy connections failing after reactor formation or controller replacement. Detached connections now safely reject transfers.\n- Fixed fusion recipes consuming incorrect quantities when ingredients were swapped, including recipes with unequal input counts.\n- Corrected dissolver output probabilities. Each output group now rolls independently, unsuccessful rolls no longer skip subsequent rolls, and zero-probability outputs cannot succeed.\n- Fixed machines continuing to use outdated or removed recipes after world loads or recipe reloads. Unchanged recipes retain their progress; changed recipes reset safely."
		},
